            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "Snow-water equivalent (SWE [m]) is computed from daily accumulation and ablation. Snow is accumulated at the rate of daily precipitation for days with a mean air temperature below a threshold of 2.8 \u00b0C (e.g., Kienzle, 2008). Snow melts based on a degree-day model (e.g., Rango and Martinec, 1995) whereby SWE is lost at a rate of 3 mm K\u22121 d\u22121 when mean daily air temperature is above 0 \u00b0C.",
